# The production build's settings (`vite build`; `build:e2e` and `vite dev` use other modes and
# never read this file, and `build:staging` reads .env.staging over it). apps/web/.env.example says
# what each one is.
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS PUBLIC. Vite compiles VITE_ values into the bundle every visitor downloads, the
# build writes the Supabase host and its own into the CSP (public/_headers, static-pages.ts), and a
# Supabase publishable key is made to ship to browsers. Never put SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY, DATABASE_URL,
# CODE_PEPPER or anything else from crates/server/.env here: env-production.test.ts fails on any key
# but these, and on a secret-shaped value.
#
# A variable already set where the build runs would win over this file (Vite never overwrites one),
# so nothing sets one: promote-production.yml builds production from this file alone, and
# apps/web/scripts/check-production-bundle.mjs refuses a bundle missing any of them, or one built with
# a variable that differs from this file's (a stale secret put staging's key here until 2026-11-04).
# Supabase: production's own project, JackiOh-Production (docs/deploy-cloudflare.md section 8).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://fuzpvmjdejvbjcarypyi.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_Wrsaw5gK4Gf_Hts0-B1skQ_DfUUUv9i
# The server shares the site's origin: wrangler.jsonc sends /api/* and /ws/* to it.
VITE_SERVER_HTTP_URL=https://jackioh.com
VITE_SERVER_WS_URL=wss://jackioh.com/ws/match
# #696: the address production is served from, named by every canonical link, og:url, sitemap entry
# and robots.txt line (static-pages.ts, net/navigate.ts siteOrigin), and the host of the CSP's socket.
VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://jackioh.com
# R666: only providers enabled in the Supabase dashboard (see .env.example). #1890: Google, enabled on
# JackiOh-Production with automatic linking on, and manual linking on for /account (R3025000). #3147:
# Roblox, the custom OIDC provider `custom:roblox` (R3147000).
VITE_AUTH_OAUTH_PROVIDERS=google,custom:roblox
# R2983000: Google's web client ID for its own button (see .env.example), the OAuth client both
# projects' Google provider uses; it lists this site as an Authorized JavaScript origin (#3026).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=93902541672-9ucch37f5sil9sjvd0im3uff6hcb77u1.apps.googleusercontent.com
